{"audio": "revelation-02.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 249600, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 2000, "text": "Revelation, Chapter Two."}, {"start_ms": 2000, "end_ms": 17600, "text": "Unto the angel of the church of Ephesus write; These things saith he that holdeth the seven stars in his right hand, who walketh in the midst of the seven golden candlesticks; I know thy works, and thy labour, and thy patience, and how thou canst not bear them which are evil:"}, {"start_ms": 17600, "end_ms": 29067, "text": "and thou hast tried them which say they are apostles, and are not, and hast found them liars: And hast borne, and hast patience, and for my name's sake hast laboured, and hast not fainted."}, {"start_ms": 29067, "end_ms": 34133, "text": "Nevertheless I have somewhat against thee, because thou hast left thy first love."}, {"start_ms": 34133, "end_ms": 46533, "text": "Remember therefore from whence thou art fallen, and repent, and do the first works; or else I will come unto thee quickly, and will remove thy candlestick out of his place, except thou repent."}, {"start_ms": 46533, "end_ms": 52400, "text": "But this thou hast, that thou hatest the deeds of the Nicolaitans, which I also hate."}, {"start_ms": 52400, "end_ms": 62933, "text": "He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches; To him that overcometh will I give to eat of the tree of life, which is in the midst of the paradise of God."}, {"start_ms": 62933, "end_ms": 79067, "text": "And unto the angel of the church in Smyrna write; These things saith the first and the last, which was dead, and is alive; I know thy works, and tribulation, and poverty, (but thou art rich) and I know the blasphemy of them which say they are Jews, and are not, but are the synagogue of Satan."}, {"start_ms": 79067, "end_ms": 91867, "text": "Fear none of those things which thou shalt suffer: behold, the devil shall cast some of you into prison, that ye may be tried; and ye shall have tribulation ten days: be thou faithful unto death, and I will give thee a crown of life."}, {"start_ms": 91867, "end_ms": 99467, "text": "He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches; He that overcometh shall not be hurt of the second death."}, {"start_ms": 99467, "end_ms": 114533, "text": "And to the angel of the church in Pergamos write; These things saith he which hath the sharp sword with two edges; I know thy works, and where thou dwellest, even where Satan's seat is: and thou holdest fast my name, and hast not denied my faith,"}, {"start_ms": 114533, "end_ms": 121333, "text": "even in those days wherein Antipas was my faithful martyr, who was slain among you, where Satan dwelleth."}, {"start_ms": 121333, "end_ms": 134533, "text": "But I have a few things against thee, because thou hast there them that hold the doctrine of Balaam, who taught Balac to cast a stumblingblock before the children of Israel, to eat things sacrificed unto idols, and to commit fornication."}, {"start_ms": 134533, "end_ms": 140533, "text": "So hast thou also them that hold the doctrine of the Nicolaitans, which thing I hate."}, {"start_ms": 140533, "end_ms": 146133, "text": "Repent; or else I will come unto thee quickly, and will fight against them with the sword of my mouth."}, {"start_ms": 146133, "end_ms": 160000, "text": "He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches; To him that overcometh will I give to eat of the hidden manna, and will give him a white stone, and in the stone a new name written, which no man knoweth saving he that receiveth it."}, {"start_ms": 160000, "end_ms": 177600, "text": "And unto the angel of the church in Thyatira write; These things saith the Son of God, who hath his eyes like unto a flame of fire, and his feet are like fine brass; I know thy works, and charity, and service, and faith, and thy patience, and thy works; and the last to be more than the first."}, {"start_ms": 177600, "end_ms": 189867, "text": "Notwithstanding I have a few things against thee, because thou sufferest that woman Jezebel, which calleth herself a prophetess, to teach and to seduce my servants to commit fornication, and to eat things sacrificed unto idols."}, {"start_ms": 189867, "end_ms": 194533, "text": "And I gave her space to repent of her fornication; and she repented not."}, {"start_ms": 194533, "end_ms": 202667, "text": "Behold, I will cast her into a bed, and them that commit adultery with her into great tribulation, except they repent of their deeds."}, {"start_ms": 202667, "end_ms": 213600, "text": "And I will kill her children with death; and all the churches shall know that I am he which searcheth the reins and hearts: and I will give unto every one of you according to your works."}, {"start_ms": 213600, "end_ms": 225333, "text": "But unto you I say, and unto the rest in Thyatira, as many as have not this doctrine, and which have not known the depths of Satan, as they speak; I will put upon you none other burden."}, {"start_ms": 225333, "end_ms": 228667, "text": "But that which ye have already hold fast till I come."}, {"start_ms": 228667, "end_ms": 242800, "text": "And he that overcometh, and keepeth my works unto the end, to him will I give power over the nations: And he shall rule them with a rod of iron; as the vessels of a potter shall they be broken to shivers: even as I received of my Father."}, {"start_ms": 242800, "end_ms": 245067, "text": "And I will give him the morning star."}, {"start_ms": 245067, "end_ms": 249600, "text": "He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches."}], "words": [{"t": "Revelation,", "s": 81, "e": 727, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 1232, "e": 1596, "si": 0}, {"t": "Two.", "s": 1657, "e": 1859, "si": 0}, {"t": "Unto", "s": 2501, "e": 2681, "si": 1}, {"t": "the", "s": 2721, "e": 2801, "si": 1}, {"t": "angel", "s": 2921, "e": 3202, "si": 1}, {"t": "of", "s": 3262, "e": 3302, "si": 1}, {"t": "the", "s": 3342, "e": 3422,